---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import GlossaryTerm from "../components/GlossaryTerm.astro";
import libraryCollection from "../assets/images/library-collection.avif";
---

<PageLayout
  title="The Library of Babble"
  description="Pre-trained language models in printed, hardbound book form — n-gram frequency tables typeset from classic literature that you can use to generate text with pen, paper, and dice."
>
  <h1>The Library of Babble</h1>

  <Image
    src={libraryCollection}
    alt="The Library of Babble collection — hardbound volumes in green, purple, brown, and blue lined up on a shelf"
    widths={[480, 960, 1440]}
    sizes="(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px"
    format="avif"
  />

  <p>
    <em>The Library of Babble</em> is a shelf of pre-trained{" "}
    <GlossaryTerm id="language-model">language models</GlossaryTerm> in printed, hardbound book
    form: each volume holds the <GlossaryTerm id="n-gram-model">n-gram</GlossaryTerm> frequency
    tables of a single literary work, so you can hold a whole model in your hands and generate text
    from it with dice. It was formerly the LLMs Unplugged Library, and it is a separate artwork from
    the teaching resources on this site.
  </p>

  <p>
    Its home is the Cybernetic Studio&rsquo;s project page,{" "}
    <a href="https://cybernetics.anu.edu.au/projects/library-of-babble/">The Library of Babble</a>,
    which describes the volumes and how they are made.
  </p>

  <p>
    To generate your own booklet from any text&mdash;in paperback PDF rather than hardbound
    form&mdash;head to the <a href="/tools/">Materials</a> page. To see the same models used in a
    teaching context, the{" "}
    <a href="/modules/pretrained-generation/">Pre-trained Model Generation</a>{" "} module walks
    through how to roll dice against a frequency table to produce new text.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
